### Data analysis and statistics

Frequency (i.e. the frequency of occurrence in the marinas where a taxa was found divided by the total number of marinas with _F. emigmaticus_) and density (i.e. number of individuals per m\({}^{-2}\)) were calculated for each taxon. For each marina, the species richness and density were studied by considering 1) the sessile fauna only; 2) the motile fauna only and 3) all species (essile + motile fauna, except _F. emigmaticus_ that cannot be counted). In addition, the Shannon diversity index (\(H\)) and evenness (_E_) were calculated as follows. \(H^{\prime}=\sum p_{i}(\log_{i}(p_{i}))\), where \(p_{i}\ =\) abundance of taxon \(i\)/total abundance; \(E=H^{\prime}/\log_{i}(S)\), where \(S\) is the species richness.

Similarity in species assemblages was investigated between pairs of marinas by computing the Screen similarity index (S\({}_{\omega}\)) (Jongman et al., 1995), as S\({}_{\omega}=2C/(A+B)\), where \(C\) is the number of species shared by the two marinas considered, and A and B the species richness of the two marinas. S\({}_{\omega}\) is expressed in percentage, and varies between 0% (no common species) and 100% (same species richness and composition).

Differences in water parameters (temperature, salinity and pH) were tested between marinas with and without _F. emigmaticus_ reefs by applying \(t\)-tests, or Mann-Whitney (M \(-\) W) tests when assumptions of normality and homoscedasticity were not met. Differences in biofouling volume and dry weight among marinas (6 groups) were analyzed with non-parametric Kruskal-Wallis (K-W) tests for the same reason. When a significant difference was detected, pairwise _post-hoc_ Dunn tests were applied to compare biofouling and dry weight among marinas.

## 3 Results

### Water parameters

Annual variability in water parameters in the marina of Carentan showed a marked seasonality in both temperature and salinity (Fig. 3). During the explorations, i.e. over the course of 2 weeks in January 2015, water temperature ranged from 6.00 \({}^{\circ}\)C \(\pm\) 0.06 SEM in the marina of Carentan (CAR) to 7.60 \({}^{\circ}\)C \(\pm\) 0.06 SEM in the outer-port basin of Chebourg (CHOP); the average temperature in the 12 marinas was 6.65 \({}^{\circ}\)C \(\pm\) 0.09 SEM. On the 8th and 9th March, the minimum and maximum values were recorded in the same marinas as during the explorations period, reaching 7.23 \({}^{\circ}\)C \(\pm\) 0.03 SEM in CAR and 8.67 \({}^{\circ}\)C \(\pm\) 0.07 SEM in CHOP, with an overall average temperature of 7.84 \({}^{\circ}\)C \(\pm\) 0.09 SEM.

